      "text": "0–10 scale combining probability × kinetic energy. Most close approaches: 0 (no concern). Apophis (2004): briefly rated 4 (worth urgent attention) before updated orbit ruled out 2029/2036 impacts. Apophis will pass at ~32,000 km in April 2029 — closer than geostationary satellites; visible to naked eye; OSIRIS-APEX mission will observe."
